This is a known breaking change in .NET 10 MAUI. Android's `adjustResize` was deprecated at the OS level, and MAUI 10 enables **edge-to-edge** mode by default, which makes `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` stop working.

## Fix: Handle keyboard insets directly

**1. In your `MainActivity.cs`, keep `adjustResize`:**

```csharp
[Activity(
    Theme = "@style/Maui.SplashTheme",
    WindowSoftInputMode = SoftInput.AdjustResize,  // still needed
    ...)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity { }
```

**2. Add an inset handler in your `MauiProgram.cs`:**

```csharp
#if ANDROID
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.LifecycleEvents;
#endif

builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android.OnCreate((activity, _) =>
    {
        var rootView = activity.Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Views.Window.IdAndroidContent)!;

        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(rootView, new KeyboardInsetsListener());
    }));
#endif
});
```

**3. Create the insets listener (in `Platforms/Android/`):**

```csharp
using AndroidX.Core.Graphics;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

public class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        // Use the larger of keyboard or nav-bar bottom inset
        int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);

        v.SetPadding(
            systemBarInsets.Left,
            systemBarInsets.Top,
            systemBarInsets.Right,
            bottomPadding);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

**How it works:** Instead of relying on the deprecated resize behavior, you listen for IME (keyboard) insets via `AndroidX.Core` and apply bottom padding to push your content up when the keyboard appears.

**iOS** doesn't need changes — MAUI still handles keyboard avoidance there automatically.
